&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid – College Park, MD&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 10%, domestic or international.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt; 1947&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Lead Accountant to join our US Accounting Team. As a Lead Accountant, you&#39;ll be part of a cross-functional team whose mission is to lead IonQ on its journey to build the world&#39;s best quantum computers to solve the world&#39;s most complex problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own the monthly, quarterly, and annual consolidation of IonQ&#39;s growing portfolio of domestic and international legal entities. This is a hands-on, player-coach position. You will run the consolidated close and prepare the consolidated financial results yourself. You will also build the processes, systems, and controls needed to consolidate a fast-growing group of acquired businesses on an accelerated public-company timeline. The ideal candidate combines deep technical knowledge of consolidation, foreign currency, and business combination accounting with strong command of consolidation systems and a drive to shorten the close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consolidated Close &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidated Close Ownership: Own the end-to-end consolidated close calendar across all IonQ legal entities. This includes running the corporate close call, tracking subsidiary deliverables and dependencies, and escalating issues that put the timeline at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidiary Reporting Packages: Set requirements for subsidiary trial balance and reporting packages, then manage their collection and review. Validate completeness, account mapping, and consistency with corporate accounting policies before data is loaded for consolidation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidation Execution: Prepare and review consolidation entries, including top-side adjustments, investment eliminations, and equity roll-forwards. Review the intercompany eliminations prepared by the Intercompany Accounting team to confirm the consolidated balances are complete and fully eliminated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidated Financial Analysis: Prepare consolidated trial balances, financial statements, and flux analyses. Investigate and explain significant movements for leadership, SEC Reporting, and FP&amp;amp;A.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consolidation, Foreign Currency &amp;amp; Acquisitions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foreign Currency Translation: Oversee translation of foreign subsidiary results under ASC 830, including exchange-rate governance, cumulative translation adjustment (CTA) roll-forwards, and related disclosure support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Combinations &amp;amp; Integration: Lead the consolidation of newly acquired and newly formed entities. This includes opening balance sheet and purchase accounting entries under ASC 805, chart of accounts mapping, reporting timelines, and onboarding local finance teams to IonQ&#39;s close requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chart of Accounts &amp;amp; Mapping Governance: Maintain the consolidated chart of accounts and the mappings from entity ledgers to the consolidation structure. Control changes so reporting stays consistent across entities and periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External Reporting Support: Supply consolidated schedules and supporting analyses for quarterly and annual SEC filings, earnings materials, and Audit Committee reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Process, Systems &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidation Systems: Serve as the accounting owner of OneStream consolidation, including workflows, data loads, validations, and consolidation and translation rules.&amp;nbsp;Systems Integration: Support data flows between NetSuite, OneStream, and downstream planning and reporting tools such as Pigment. Make sure the consolidated results reconcile to the source ledgers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Design: Build and document scalable consolidation processes, close calendars, and reporting package standards that reduce manual effort and shorten the close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous Improvement: Find the root causes of recurring consolidation adjustments and late or inaccurate submissions, and fix them upstream with entity controllers and shared services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Controls, Audit &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal Controls: Design, document, and execute internal controls over the consolidation and financial reporting processes. Remediate control gaps as the control environment grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit Support: Serve as the primary consolidation contact for external auditors. Prepare consolidation schedules, roll-forwards, and supporting documentation (PBC list items) for quarterly reviews and the year-end audit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Accounting: Research and document accounting positions on consolidation, foreign currency, and business combination matters under US GAAP (ASC 805, ASC 810, ASC 830). Monitor policy compliance across entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/BA in Accounting or Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of progressive accounting experience, including consolidation accounting in a multi-entity, multi-currency environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience owning or leading a consolidated monthly and quarterly close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of US GAAP, including consolidation (ASC 810), foreign currency (ASC 830), and business combinations (ASC 805)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating internal controls in a SOX or SOX-readiness environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including the ability to work with large data sets and build repeatable analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to coordinate deadlines and requirements with finance teams across geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and self-motivated, with the ability to meet deadlines and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA or equivalent certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a Big Four accounting firm or other national accounting firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with OneStream (or a comparable consolidation system) and NetSuite, particularly OneWorld and multi-book accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public company experience, including SEC reporting timelines and SOX 404 compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating newly acquired entities into an existing accounting and consolidation structure, including purchase accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing or improving a consolidation system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success automating manual accounting processes and reducing close cycle time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to take on challenges and think constructively to solve problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base, bonus, equity, and a range of benefit options found on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;If this role has a commission structure, the compensation range below just reflects the base compensation range.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Wage Transparency:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$92,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$138,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
