&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Receiving Inspector to join our Quality team. As a Senior Receiving Inspector, you’ll be part of a cross-functional team whose mission is to lead IonQ on its journey to build the world’s best quantum computers to solve the world’s most complex problems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will make sure that incoming, in-process, and finished components agree with mechanical, electrical, and PCBA specifications. You will also own the inspection element of the Material Review Board (MRB) process: the handling and the containment of nonconforming material, the inspection actions that the MRB assigns, and the verification, closure, and tracking of nonconformance records after the Quality Engineer gives the disposition. You will serve as the senior technical resource for inspection, allocate daily inspection work, and give guidance to less-experienced inspectors. The ideal candidate balances technical expertise with the professional integrity to hold quality standards under production pressure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily inspection of incoming parts, in-process production, and final release of finished goods. Determine the inspection method and the sequence of daily work with little instruction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect mechanical, electrical, and PCBA components and their documentation against approved engineering specifications, drawings, and purchase order requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret drawing callouts and datum structures (GD&amp;amp;T, ASME Y14.5), and convert them into inspection plans and acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply statistical sampling plans to select the sample size and the acceptance criteria, and increase the sample size when the quality data shows a risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select and use the correct metrology gauges and instruments, and program and operate automated measurement systems (CMM, OMM, or vision systems).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the calibration schedule. Remove out-of-tolerance equipment from service and start the recall and impact assessment for affected product. Keep the inspection area and the tooling to the local 5S procedure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Control nonconforming material. Identify, tag, segregate, and quarantine the material, and keep lot and serial traceability correct at each move (ISO 9001, AS9100).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do the containment actions. Sweep stock, work-in-process, in-transit, and finished goods to find all affected material, and hold the affected lots until the disposition is complete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write the nonconformance record (NCR) for Material Review Board review with the nonconforming condition, the measurement data, the affected quantity, the traceability data, and photographs, and present the inspection evidence at the MRB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do the inspection actions that the MRB assigns, including 100% screen, sort, re-inspection, expanded sampling, and verification of rework or repair against the approved disposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify and close nonconformance records after the Quality Engineer gives the disposition. Confirm that the disposition is complete and that the objective evidence is in the record. The Quality Engineer holds the disposition authority; refer each condition that does not agree with the disposition back to the Quality Engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track the MRB closure action items. Keep the MRB log and the aging report, follow up with the action owners, report open and overdue items at the quality meeting, and escalate items at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify the mutilation and the disposal of scrapped material so that it cannot return to the supply chain and to prevent counterfeit parts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give the inspection data from non conformances to the Quality Engineer to support root cause analysis, corrective action, and supplier corrective action requests (SCARs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, and release inspection procedures and work instructions in the document control system. Analyze inspection and nonconformance data, and issue metrics for first pass yield, defect Pareto, NCR aging, and inspection turnaround time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the lead inspector. Allocate the daily inspection workload, train and give technical guidance to less-experienced inspectors, verify their inspection results and nonconformance records before release, and propose improvements to inspection methods, tooling, and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineering, manufacturing, supply chain, suppliers, and calibration and test laboratories to resolve quality problems and to complete source inspection and first article inspection activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal, customer, and regulatory audits as the subject matter resource for inspection and for the control of nonconforming outputs, and give the inspection position at change reviews for proposed process and design changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep compliance with quality management system, export control, and customer contract requirements for the handling, the marking, and the storage of controlled material and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High School Diploma (or equivalent) with 6 or more years of related experience in a regulated manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in PCBA inspection to IPC-A-610 requirements, and with aerospace inspection processes and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with the control of nonconforming product and with the Material Review Board process, including material identification and segregation, containment, assigned inspection actions, and the verification and closure of nonconformance records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a Quality Management System (QMS) or ERP nonconformance module for the creation, the tracking, and the closure of nonconformance records and action items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience to allocate work to, to train, and to give technical guidance to less-experienced inspectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret complex technical drawings, including a thorough understanding of datum structures per ASME Y14.5.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level proficiency with layout tools (surface plates, height gages, indicators, calipers, micrometers, gage blocks, and thread gages).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid proficiency in standard office software for data analysis, document creation, and scheduling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 40 pounds (18 kg) and to stand for extended periods during inspection cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strict adherence to all company safety requirements and PPE protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicates effectively at all organizational levels, which includes management, engineering, and physicists, to resolve complex quality issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of root cause analysis and problem solving methods (5-Why, Ishikawa, or 8D) to support the Quality Engineer during nonconformance investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with first article inspection (AS9102) and with source inspection at supplier sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification as an ASQ Certified Quality Inspector (CQI), Certified Quality Technician (CQT), or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A quality-first mindset with a proven record of precision, and the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who is willing to learn, to grow, and to support other QA functions as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;The total compensation package includes base, bonus, equity, and a range of benefit options found on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This role is non-exempt and eligible for overtime in accordance with company policies. The listed pay range below reflects the base hourly rate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this role has a commission structure, the compensation range below just reflects the base compensation range.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Hourly Wage Transparency&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$32&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$49 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Oxford, England, UK&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working pattern:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Silicon Validation Engineer to join our Cryo-CMOS IC team at IonQ Oxford. You will lead the validation and characterisation of analogue and mixed-signal ASICs for our trapped-ion quantum processors, from test planning and platform development through first-silicon bring-up, debug and system integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on technical role. You will shape our validation architecture, build reusable hardware and software, and provide the evidence needed to make confident silicon acceptance decisions. The work includes room-temperature silicon validation and silicon characterisation at cryogenic temperatures (around 4 kelvin), on packaged parts, chip-on-board assemblies and bare die on a cryogenic probe station.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own validation delivery across chip and system interfaces, working closely with analogue and digital design, verification, modelling, firmware and systems engineers. You will turn requirements into measurable tests, prepare platforms before silicon arrives and resolve failures across the chip, board and software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior engineer, you will set technical standards, guide other engineers and improve coverage, repeatability and test efficiency across successive ASIC generations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the silicon validation strategy, plans, acceptance criteria and readiness reviews, with traceability from block and system requirements to tests, results and unresolved risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Present the silicon acceptance report to the Cryo-CMOS IC Lead and programme stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead first-silicon bring-up and characterisation of sample-and-hold and switch arrays, DACs, ADCs, references, amplifiers, switches, regulators, clocking and device-level test structures, across supply, temperature, operating modes and device variation, with sound calibration and measurement uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop validation boards, fixtures and reusable Python automation, instrument drivers and regression suites, addressing signal integrity, grounding, power integrity and measurement access, with version-controlled tests and reproducible data analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Plan and lead cryogenic measurements with specialist colleagues, including bare-die probing and the cold signal chain, and drive failures to root cause, separating silicon defects from board, firmware and test artefacts and correlating results with simulations, device models and foundry or partner data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Influence testability before tape-out, coordinate validation with external design partners, the foundry and other IonQ sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead technical reviews, mentor engineers and document methods to improve throughput, data quality and reuse.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bring substantial experience in analogue or mixed-signal silicon validation and characterisation, with ownership of multiple silicon bring-up programmes. A degree in electrical or electronic engineering, or equivalent practical experience, is expected. You should combine hands-on laboratory skills with sound judgement on test coverage, measurement confidence and programme risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong electronics fundamentals and experience validating precision signal chains, data converters or power-management circuits, including their digital control interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Practical expertise with oscilloscopes, precision sources and meters, signal generators, spectrum and logic analysers; confidence designing reliable low-noise, low-leakage measurements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong Python programming for instrument control, automated testing and statistical analysis; disciplined use of Git or equivalent version control and maintainable test software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience designing and debugging test PCBs, reviewing layouts and working with interfaces such as SPI, I2C, JTAG and custom shift-register chains, alongside embedded firmware or FPGA-based platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A record of resolving complex chip, board and software interactions through structured experiments and collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading technical projects, mentoring engineers and communicating evidence, uncertainty and decisions in clear written reports.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Useful additional experience includes cryogenic or other extreme-temperature testing; wafer or bare-die probing; early-stage IP or test-chip evaluation; FPGA development and C/C++; circuit simulation; and production test correlation. Prior quantum computing is welcome but not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be part of a team that’s shaping the future of quantum. We offer more than just a role, you’ll join a world class community of scientists, engineers and innovators working to unlock the full potential of quantum computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a range of benefits, including opportunities to further your career alongside industry leaders, a competitive salary with IonQ stock options, an annual performance bonus, generous annual leave, flexible hybrid working, private medical and dental insurance for you and your family, and much more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and be part of the future of quantum computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and welcome applicants from all backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is based at our Bothell, WA office, with the option to work a few days a week remotely.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; 1734&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a senior software engineering manager to lead and grow our developer tools team. In this role, you’ll help deliver access to our industry-leading quantum computers and simulators via software development kits (SDKs) that make programming them a delight. You’ll regularly engage with the developer community to stay up to date with trends in industry and research communities alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have experience leading or contributing to multiple simultaneous initiatives, balancing multiple activities with a keen eye for prioritizing for the biggest impact. You’ll be able to balance technical expertise and savvy with strong business judgment to make great technology choices with lasting impact. You’ll strive for simplicity and demonstrate significant creativity and incisive judgment. You&#39;ll enjoy learning technical topics, working across multiple business streams, and be uniquely positioned to help us reach the next horizon in secure quantum computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of software engineers creating SDKs and libraries for programming quantum computers and interacting with the systems and services around them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our codebase not as the lead developer, but to remain connected to the work your team is doing as a player-coach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in developer forums and events to keep your finger on the pulse of this rapidly evolving field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical expertise and strong thought leadership in building robust, well-engineered, and scalable software solutions, participating in code reviews and ensuring best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive functional and technical delivery of key team and org-wide programs/initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers, Product Managers, and other cross functional partners to define, scope, and drive large programs to conclusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and iterate on program management techniques, frameworks, and KPIs to achieve goals with well defined success criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and produce high quality written proposals, communications and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create widely circulated plans, driving consistency, clarity and building alignment across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help influence peers / leaders and build consensus while dealing with ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In your first three months, you’ll be helping hire key staff to scale this function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Physics, or related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of hands-on technical leadership and people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience of open source contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience of programming experience in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past experience building SDKs, and ideally those built for use in hybrid cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in quantum computing SDKs (Qiskit, Pennylane, CirQ)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of team management best practices and demonstrated experience building and scaling effective teams that drives a high performance culture in a distributed work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills with the ability to partner and align with external software teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound project management, analytical skills and ability to establish metrics to measure and drive a high return on investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in modern software development practices and tools (e.g., continuous integration and delivery, observability, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client focus and the ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with internal and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS or PhD in Computer Science, Physics, Quantum Information Science, or a related degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technical leadership and people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of managing distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an open source project maintainer with an active community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in quantum computing and/or quantum information science&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;The approximate base salary range for this position is &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;$200,698&lt;/span&gt; -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;$262,765&lt;/span&gt;. The total compensation package includes base, bonus, equity, and a range of benefit options found on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Oxford, UK&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Office commitment:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quantum is now, and it&#39;s built here. Oxford Ionics, now part of IonQ, is pioneering the next generation of quantum computing. Using our world-leading trapped-ion technology, we&#39;re building the most powerful, accurate and reliable quantum systems to tackle problems that today&#39;s supercomputers cannot solve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an enthusiastic and highly technical Senior Software Engineer for our non-realtime controllers team who will thrive in our dynamic cross-disciplinary environment. You will be working closely with our skilled software engineers, our systems teams who operate the physical quantum computers, and our world-leading quantum scientists to build and operate the software that controls the hardware surrounding our quantum computers. Previous exposure to quantum systems is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own areas of the hardware control surface end to end, from the device protocol up to a service running reliably across our fleet. This is a hands-on engineering role and stays that way as you grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A working quantum computer is far more than the ion trap and its real-time control electronics. It depends on a fleet of supporting hardware, including cryogenic compressors, vacuum pumps, power supplies, lasers, temperature controllers, wavemeters and cameras, that has to be kept observable, controllable and reliable. The timing-critical operations such as gate waveforms and ion transport run on dedicated real-time FPGA systems, while this team owns everything that does not need hard timing guarantees. These services run on general-purpose Linux hardware and must be rock-solid, because a failed compressor or an un-noticed pressure drift takes a whole machine offline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on engineering role, balancing delivery of your own areas with support for the teams and scientists who depend on them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a group of device controllers end to end, covering API design, implementation, rollout and ongoing operational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make services robust against the ways real instruments fail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring devices onto our current framework, and roll the result out across the fleet without disrupting running experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the shared framework where a problem turns out to be common to many controllers rather than specific to one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the systems teams and scientists who depend on these services, and strengthen observability, health checking and alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the standard of the code around you through review, and bring less experienced engineers on by working alongside them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be successful, you will need experience working with Linux based systems and interfacing with hardware, and a track record of making software behave well against unreliable external dependencies. We&#39;re looking for someone who can own a problem area with little supervision and judge where robustness is worth the effort.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems engineering skills. Our controllers are written in Rust, so either solid Rust experience or deep proficiency in another systems language and the appetite to work in a Rust codebase, including async programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating networked services such as gRPC or REST, with a real grasp of error handling, observability and failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of hardware and instrument protocols and interfaces such as SCPI, Modbus, serial and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable owning the production behaviour of what you build, not just its correctness in test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills both within software and across disciplines, and an interest in helping other engineers get better at the craft without wanting to stop building yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be part of a team that’s shaping the future of quantum. We offer more than just a role, you’ll join a world class community of scientists, engineers and innovators working to unlock the full potential of quantum computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a range of benefits, including opportunities to further your career alongside industry leaders, a competitive salary with IonQ stock options, an annual performance bonus, generous annual leave, flexible hybrid working, private medical and dental insurance for you and your family, and much more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and be part of the future of quantum computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and welcome applicants from all backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Oxford, UK&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Job ID:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; 1831&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our Runtime Software team at Oxford Ionics / IonQ. In this role, you will be responsible for working directly with the experimental scientists to implement the real-time control system behaviours and provide abstractions they require for their experiments, contributing to the team’s mission of enabling our science teams to experiment and improve the primitive operations which allow compute, and building towards fault tolerant computation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll play an important part in shaping the core, Rust, libraries and the execution environment which take our system from a collection of hardware to a quantum computer, and support our work in building the world’s most advanced quantum systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this position, you will work on developing abstractions over real-time control hardware, supporting the effective delivery of a control system capable of repeatedly and reproducibly driving our ions with nano-second level precision, with abstractions which are conducive to both fast iteration and system scaling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll have the opportunity to accelerate the science core to the development of our systems, and contribute to the core execution model of our quantum computers, contributing directly to the success of building utility-scale quantum computers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with scientists to understand their requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interfacing with system orchestration, non-realtime control and compiler teams to ensure our work integrates seamlessly with the wider software architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implementing drivers for various real-time devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Producing tooling to enable users of our code to iterate rapidly and fearlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing the execution environment for the user programs which run on our systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually improving the APIs used by our internal users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be successful, you will need expert programming skills in a systems programming language and a desire to produce high quality code appropriate to a real-time environment. We’re looking for someone who can quickly iterate on low-level code in a collaborative, cross-disciplinary, environment and contribute effectively within a fast moving, highly technical team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’d be a great fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong programming skills in one or more mainstream programming languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with a systems programming programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an interest in or experience with Rust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have developed excellent communication skills both within the context of software and across disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable working with rapidly evolving requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are used to maintaining and producing high quality code reviews and appropriate testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a desire to maximize impact through quick iteration and short cycles of learning and improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are eager to learn and develop your skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
