&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IonQ is building quantum computers that change which problems the world can solve. Our Control Electronics team creates every custom electronic device inside an IonQ system, taking the hardware, gateware, firmware and test behind the precision control boards around the ion trap from development through to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Technical Programme Manager for Electrical Engineering, you will drive the team&#39;s workstreams, working directly with the programme lead TPM in our Programme Management Office. You will sit at the centre of a cross-functional group of engineers and physicists, turning complex technical work into clear plans, measurable milestones and predictable delivery for our quantum computing roadmap. This is a hands-on role that takes real weight off our design engineers, so they can stay focused on design and the bench.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will create and run the operating rhythm that keeps teams aligned and leaders informed: building development plans and an integrated schedule, tracking dependencies and surfacing risk early. You do not need to be the designer, but you need to be technical enough not to be fooled. When an estimate looks too long or a fix is always two days away, you will know which questions to ask, bring in the right architect or physicist, and turn the answer into a realistic plan with the right number of steps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Much of the help the team needs sits between functions. You will be the link between design engineering, procurement, materials management, supply chain, NPI and production, organising orders, parts and boards so that engineers handle the technical questions and the logistics are handled for them. When a component has a long lead time, you will understand its key characteristics well enough to help find an alternative. You will also keep embedded software, systems architecture and physics requirements in step with the electronics plan, represent the team&#39;s progress in programme meetings so that leads do not have to attend every one, and travel up to 20% of the time to partner sites as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the control electronics workstreams across hardware, gateware, firmware and test, owning schedule, resources, dependencies and stakeholder alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a realistic integrated schedule, challenging estimates and surfacing technical and schedule risk early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate orders, parts and boards with procurement, materials management and suppliers, and help resolve long lead and obsolete component issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional execution with physics, systems, embedded software, NPI and production teams, taking issues to closure with clear mitigation plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish programme cadences and executive reporting, including dashboards, status updates and decision logs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a technically fluent programme manager with genuine hardware programme experience, who brings structure, pace and precision to complex electronics work. You will have run, or worked closely inside, the full hardware lifecycle, including firmware and lower level test, from requirements and design through fabrication, bring-up and revision into production. You will have enough exposure to firmware or RTL work to judge whether an estimate is realistic, even if you have not written that code yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bring a degree in electrical engineering or a related technical field, and an advanced degree is a plus. You will be comfortable working day to day with physicists and engineers, building trust quickly, and translating progress, risks and trade-offs into clear, decision-ready reporting for senior stakeholders. You thrive in ambiguity, can spot inconsistencies in messy data, and enjoy both sides of the job: getting into the detail of procurement and tracking, and knowing when to take a technical discussion offline with the right people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a technical programme manager delivering complex electronics hardware programmes from development into production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in electrical engineering or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of firmware, gateware or RTL development and lower level hardware test&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing procurement, component sourcing and supplier issues for prototype or low-volume builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with modern programme tools such as Jira, Confluence, Smartsheet and GitHub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base salary, bonus, equity, and a range of benefits available on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;If this role has a commission structure, the compensation range below just reflects the base compensation range.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Wage Transparency:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$228,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Role:&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Technical Programme Manager to lead the delivery of IonQ&#39;s quantum computing systems to customer sites across Europe and Asia. You will own deployment and commissioning end to end, from early planning and export through to installation, commissioning and customer handover.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You will work across engineering, science, global mobility, legal and trade compliance, supply chain, logistics, facilities, security and customer teams. We are growing quickly and the support functions a programme manager finds at a larger company are still being built here, so the role suits someone who takes ownership, designs the process where none exists, and sweats the detail themselves.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this position, you will plan and run quantum system deployments at customer sites across Europe and Asia, with the first installations already in view.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You will have the opportunity to define how delivery works at IonQ rather than inherit it, working alongside the manufacturing and deployment programme based in Bothell.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead planning and execution of quantum system deployment and commissioning at customer sites across Europe and Asia.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Run export, import and customs work with legal, trade compliance and logistics teams for highly specialised equipment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coordinate global mobility for deploying teams, covering visas, work authorisation, travel and field assignment readiness.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Drive site readiness with facilities, security, networking and customer stakeholders, and coordinate staffing, installation sequencing and vendors onsite.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Track risk and critical path, and resolve issues across internal teams, vendors and customers.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To be successful, you will come from a hardware background, with five or more years running technical programmes or deployments of complex hardware systems, and a technical degree or equivalent experience. You will have moved equipment and people across borders before, so export, customs and visas are familiar ground rather than a surprise. You will be comfortable holding a critical path across teams that do not report to you, and able to explain technical status clearly to engineers, executives and customers alike. The role involves travel of around 10% to 20%, depending on deployment schedules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a first of its kind product from prototype into production.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Installing or commissioning complex hardware at customer sites internationally.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Work with enterprise, government or research customers during onsite deployment.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A second European language, or exposure to trapped ion systems, photonics or quantum computing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base salary, bonus, equity, and a range of benefits available on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
